<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of New South Wales</h1><p class="st-meta">1788 CE – 1901 CE · capital Sydney</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first British colony in Australia, founded as a penal settlement at Sydney Cove in 1788 and the parent of every other Australian colony.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After losing the American colonies as a destination for convicts, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> sent the First Fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-phillip">Arthur Phillip</a>, which landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-cove">Sydney Cove</a> in January 1788. The colony initially claimed the whole eastern half of the continent, from which <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-tasmania">Tasmania</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-south-australia">South Australia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-victoria">Victoria</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-queensland">Queensland</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> were later separated.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Early New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a> was a military-run penal colony, troubled by famine and by the officers' rum trade that ended in the deposition of Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-bligh">William Bligh</a> in 1808. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lachlan-macquarie">Lachlan Macquarie</a> built roads and public buildings and promoted freed convicts. Fine merino wool became the staple export, and the gold rush of 1851 brought free migrants. Expansion dispossessed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aboriginal-australians">Aboriginal</a> nations through violence and disease. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penal-transportation">Transportation</a> ended in 1840, and self-government came in 1856.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under premiers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-parkes">Henry Parkes</a>, a leading advocate of federation, New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a> joined the other colonies to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia">Commonwealth of Australia</a> on 1 January 1901, becoming a state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/colony-of-new-south-wales.jpg" alt="Colony of New South Wales" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Denelson83 (original) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_South_Wales.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1788 CE – 1901 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sydney</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Arthur Phillip, Lachlan Macquarie, Henry Parkes</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism, Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/australia">Australia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>New South Wales</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1844&amp;focus=colony-of-new-south-wales" aria-label="Colony of New South Wales on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8536 3405 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of New South Wales lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8856 3661L9384 3761M8856 3661L4997 651M8856 3661L4997 651M8856 3661L8774 3709M8856 3661L8559 3957M8856 3661L8617 3793M8856 3661L9020 3441"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M9384 3761h0M4997 651h0M4997 651h0M8774 3709h0M8559 3957h0M8617 3793h0M9020 3441h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8856 3661h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8856 3661h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sydney. <a href="/atlas?year=1844&amp;focus=colony-of-new-south-wales">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
